#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ csubraw.apls -- Dyalog APL, element-by-element loop (2026).
⍝ Keith's kernel written as explicit :For loops over a ny×nx matrix, the
⍝ form APL is not designed for; csubary.apls is the one-line array form.
⍝ The input is offset by 0.5 so it stays floating point: Dyalog stores
⍝ whole-number floats as integers, which would turn this into an integer
⍝ test. Run as
⍝    dyalogscript csubraw.apls 100 2000 10
⎕IO←0
∇ out←csub(in nx ny out);ix;iy
  :For iy :In ⍳ny
      :For ix :In ⍳nx
          out[iy;ix]←in[iy;ix]+ix+iy
      :EndFor
  :EndFor
∇
args←2⎕NQ#'GetCommandLineArgs'
(nrpt nx ny)←⍎¨¯3↑(1↓args),(0⌈4-≢args)↑'100' '2000' '10'
in←0.5+(nx+ny)-(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
out←ny nx⍴0.5
⎕←'Arrays ',(⍕nx),' by ',(⍕ny),' count ',⍕nrpt
:For r :In ⍳nrpt
    out←csub in nx ny out
:EndFor
:If ∨/,out≠in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
    ⎕←'Error: result does not match'
:EndIf
